      "extract": "Young diagrams and symmetric functions 2.1 Young diagrams We consider partitions of non-negative integers where the summands are in non- strictly decreasing order. We consider partitions to be equal if they diﬀer only by a number of zero-summands at the end. A Young diagram is a graphical depiction of a partition. A partition λ = (λ1, λ2, . . . , λk) becomes a ﬂush-left arrangement of square cells with λ1 cells in",
