      "extract": "We consider a rectangle F with n outgoing points at the top and n incoming points at the bottom, n ≥0. We denote the Homﬂy skein of this surface by Rn n. It is known to be isomorphic to the Hecke algebra Hn. Rn n gets an algebra structure by deﬁning D · E as putting D above E so that the incoming points of D match with the outgoing points of E. Clearly, Rn n is generated as an algebra by the elementary braids σ1, .",
