      "extract": "The skein C of the annulus The skein of the annulus shall be denoted by C. Let D1 and D2 be two diagrams in the annulus S1×[0, 1]. We can bring D1 into S1×[0, 1/2), and D2 into S1×(1/2, 1] by regular isotopies. Then the product of D1 and D2 is deﬁned as the diagram D1 ∪D2. An example is shown in ﬁgure 2. The product is commutative since D1D2 and D2D1 diﬀer by regular isotopy. The empty diagram is the identity. 4 Γ",
